// Cross-corpus paraphrases: the set where a model earns its place.
//
// A row here describes a thing in a visitor's words, never the author's. No
// alias of the expected answer and no word of its title may appear
// verbatim -- `atlas-questions` enforces that against the corpus, because a
// drafter cannot hold every alias of 643 resources in mind. A question that
// contains its own answer measures lookup, not understanding, and the
// matcher wins those by construction.
//
// Every row below was drafted by a model on 2026-09-22 and is Unconfirmed.
// None of them is a yardstick until the repository owner has passed over
// it. Confirm by changing status to Confirmed; reject by deleting the row
// and, where it is worth saying, leaving its note behind as a comment.
//
// The set is frozen by the hash `just questions` prints. Adding or editing
// a row changes that hash, which is the point: a set that changed after a
// measurement is not the set that measurement was made against.
QuestionSet(
    name: "paraphrase",
    note: "Phrasings that share no alias and no title word with their answer. Target: at least 300 confirmed rows before any model is trained. Drafted in batches; batch 1 is 112 rows across every resource kind.",
    rows: [
        // --- the 1960s machines, the wing and its exhibits ---
        (text: "the machine with the toggle switches and the row of little lights", expect: ["campus:ibm-1130"], intent: Navigate, origin: Teacher, status: Unconfirmed, note: "the console panel, described by someone who saw a photo"),
        (text: "i want to flip switches on an old mainframe in my browser", expect: ["campus:ibm-1130-emulator"], intent: Navigate, origin: Teacher, status: Unconfirmed, note: ""),
        (text: "which exhibit lets me run a program on a machine from before floppy disks", expect: ["campus:ibm-1130-emulator"], intent: FindResource, origin: Teacher, status: Unconfirmed, note: ""),
